        /// Default mapping established from the IDEA Checkbot OpenModel results:
        /// IDEA x = STAAD x, IDEA y = STAAD z, IDEA z = -STAAD y.
        /// This is a proper +90-degree rotation about local x and preserves a
        /// right-handed basis. It reproduces IDEA's imported N/Qy/Qz/Mx/My/Mz
        /// values for both member incidences in the reference STAAD model.
        /// </summary>

/// <summary>
        /// IDEA structural-result bending-component convention verified against
        /// Checkbot: IDEA Mx = STAAD Mx, IDEA My = STAAD Mz, IDEA Mz = STAAD My.
        /// Unlike a physical vector rotation this is an orthogonal convention map
        /// with determinant -1 because IDEA's bending-result signs are defined by
        /// fibre tension, not solely by coordinate-vector rotation.
        /// </summary>

